[AttributeError: Trial metadata access] (noted by Claude): 2026-09-04

Incident: AttributeError when processing trials during summarize_results

Error:
AttributeError: 'Trial' object has no attribute 'model'

Context:
In _track_item_level_issues, _track_repeated_sequence_issue, and _track_format_level_issues in trial_loading.py, code attempted to access trial.model, trial.temperature, trial.prompt directly as attributes. But Trial dataclass only has: filename, file_type, extension, items, metadata.

Root cause:
When moving functions from summarize.py to trial_loading.py, forgot to update attribute access from direct (trial.model) to dict access (trial.metadata.get("model")).

Resolution:
Updated all three tracking functions to extract model, temperature, and prompt from trial.metadata dict instead of accessing as direct attributes. TrialKey now constructed correctly from metadata values.

